Adverse Events
The following and further adverse events may occur during or despite the appliance of the pRESET:
• Air-, catheter-, plaque-, thrombus-emboli;
• Allergic/toxic reaction;
• Adverse response by patient including reaction to antiplatelet/anticoagulation or contrast media;
• Arteriovenous fistula;
• Brain edema;
• Death;
• Device deformation, collapse, fracture or malfunction;
• Distal embolization to previously uninvolved territory;
• Extracranial hemorrhage;
• Extracranial/intracranial complications during procedure;
• Hematoma and hemorrhage at puncture site;
• Infection;
• Inflammation;
• Ischemic stroke/hemorrhagic stroke;
• Neurovascular/neurological complications;
• Pain/headache;
• Pseudoaneurysm formation;
• Post-procedure bleeding;
• Severe harm (permanent disability/death);
• Thrombosis (acute and subacute);
• Vasospasm;
• Vessel perforation/occlusion/dissection/thrombosis/damage.
Note: This device requires the use with fluoroscopy. X-ray radiation exposure may cause adverse events including, but not
limited to, alopecia, burns, cataracts, or delayed neoplasia (cancers). The probability of occurrence of complications may
increase as procedure time and number of procedures increases.
